    <person:biography visibility="public">
        <common:created-date>2025-03-03T19:41:28.115Z</common:created-date>
        <common:last-modified-date>2025-03-03T19:41:28.115Z</common:last-modified-date>
        <personal-details:content>Kalyani Dhusia, Ph.D. is a Bioinformatics Scientist with extensive experience in genomics, computational biology, and machine learning. She holds a Ph.D. in Bioinformatics and currently serves as an Assistant Staff Scientist at the University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences (UAMS). Dr. Dhusia specializes in developing and optimizing bioinformatics pipelines for analyzing large-scale genomic, proteomics and multi-omic datasets. Her work focuses on precision medicine, cancer genomics, and epigenetic analysis, utilizing tools like Python, R, Nextflow, and GCP. She has contributed to numerous research projects and publications, demonstrating a strong ability to collaborate across interdisciplinary teams to advance biomedical research.</personal-details:content>
    </person:biography>
